3′ path</data><data key="n_note">The longer V 3′ primary contig runs through this fragment. Repeat homology continues toward the V_unloc_1 cap candidate.</data><data key="n_span">104342</data><data key="n_orientation">Native fragment coordinate from its 5′ end</data><data key="n_tracks">[{"family":"p177","arrays":[{"start":2560,"end":96960,"periods":[82,177],"evidence":["TRF","marker span"],"annotations":["sat_fam06","sat_fam07"]}],"total":94400},{"family":"p20","arrays":[{"start":0,"end":640,"periods":[20],"evidence":["marker span"],"annotations":[]},{"start":2240,"end":2880,"periods":[20],"evidence":["marker span"],"annotations":[]}],"total":1280}]</data></node><node id="G_C38"><data key="n_label">C000038 cap fragment</data><data key="n_type">graph</data><data key="n_status">Capped graph fragment</data><data key="n_note">Primary unitig utg000068l and primary contig ptg000020l describe the same 202,511 bp path. Full HiFi reads support the telomere junction. Its opposite edge matches the III 5′ and V 3′ repeat.</data><data key="n_span">202511</data><data key="n_orientation">From the candidate outward edge inward</data><data key="n_tracks">[{"family":"p20","arrays":[{"start":129280,"end":202400,"periods":[20],"evidence":["marker span"],"annotations":[]}],"total":73120}]</data></node><node id="G_V3"><data key="n_label">Long V 3′ path</data><data key="n_type">graph</data><data key="n_status">Graph candidate</data><data key="n_note">Distal 165,508 bp of the longer V 3′ primary contig, shown from its candidate tip inward. It includes V_unloc_2. Raw utg000162l reproduces the last 33 kb in the corresponding orientation.</data><data key="n_span">165508</data><data key="n_orientation">From the candidate outward edge inward</data><data key="n_tracks">[{"family":"p177","arrays":[{"start":14560,"end":108960,"periods":[177],"evidence":["marker span"],"annotations":[]}],"total":94400},{"family":"p20","arrays":[{"start":0,"end":12640,"periods":[20],"evidence":["marker span"],"annotations":[]},{"start":14240,"end":14880,"periods":[20],"evidence":["marker span"],"annotations":[]}],"total":13280}]</data></node><node id="G_II5"><data key="n_label">Farther II path</data><data key="n_type">graph</data><data key="n_status">Graph candidate</data><data key="n_note">Primary unitig utg000063l contains reversed II_unloc_4 and part of II_unloc_2. Native 5′ position is the proposed farther outward side. The join to the latest II tip remains unresolved.</data><data key="n_span">106055</data><data key="n_orientation">From the candidate outward edge inward</data><data key="n_tracks">[{"family":"mix","arrays":[{"start":50400,"end":105920,"periods":[191],"evidence":["marker span"],"annotations":[]}],"total":55520}]</data></node><node id="G_I3"><data key="n_label">Long I 3′ allele</data><data key="n_type">graph</data><data key="n_status">Alternate cap path</data><data key="n_note">Last 85 kb of primary contig ptg000013l, shown from its candidate distal tip inward. A longer alternative supported by C000028. The reviewed I 3′ end uses C000043.</data><data key="n_span">85000</data><data key="n_orientation">From the candidate outward edge inward</data><data key="n_tracks">[{"family":"p96","arrays":[{"start":81600,"end":84960,"periods":[96],"evidence":["marker span"],"annotations":[]}],"total":3360}]</data></node><node id="mix"><data key="n_label">175–343 bp mixed</data><data key="n_type">repeat</data><data key="n_note">A broad satellite group with distinct short units, 343 bp arrays and longer combinations. X 5′ is dominated by a 343 bp variant. X 3′ and the extended II 5′ tip have mixed architectures.</data><data key="n_period">175,188,191,194,343</data></node><node id="p20"><data key="n_label">20 bp array</data><data key="n_type">repeat</data><data key="n_note">The outer III 5′ repeat. Longer candidate paths on III and V share its markers. Placement depends on the adjoining unique flanks and the orientation of the repeat.</data><data key="n_period">20</data></node><node id="p23"><data key="n_label">23 bp array</data><data key="n_type">repeat</data><data key="n_note">The former II 5′ port. A matching array at the 3′ edge of II_unloc_3 is bridged by four ONT reads. The repeat is now internal to the extended II 5′ arm.</data><data key="n_period">23</data></node><node id="p96"><data key="n_label">~95 bp array</data><data key="n_type">repeat</data><data key="n_note">Two overlapping family labels describe a related repeat with 32 bp periodicity in parts of the II arrays.</data><data key="n_period">32,94,95,96</data></node><node id="p177"><data key="n_label">82 / 177 bp arrays</data><data key="n_type">repeat</data><data key="n_note">Overlapping family labels for a mixed satellite. A large block lies inward of III 5′, with related sequence on the V route and II 3′.</data><data key="n_period">82,85,168,177</data></node><node id="p87"><data key="n_label">87 bp array</data><data key="n_type">repeat</data><data key="n_note">Satellite family sat_fam08.</data><data key="n_period">87</data></node><node id="p81"><data key="n_label">81 bp array</data><data key="n_type">repeat</data><data key="n_note">Satellite family sat_fam10.</data><data key="n_period">81</data></node><node id="p69"><data key="n_label">69 bp arrays</data><data key="n_type">repeat</data><data key="n_note">Related 69 bp annotations sat_fam11 and sat_fam12.</data><data key="n_period">69</data></node><edge id="e1" source="I_5p" target="mix"><data key="e_kind">array</data><data key="e_label">Satellite occurrence</data><data key="e_span">111360</data><data key="e_note">Annotated arrays and/or contiguous windows carrying recurrent family markers.</data></edge><edge id="e2" source="I_5p" target="p20"><data key="e_kind">array</data><data key="e_label">Satellite occurrence</data><data key="e_span">35680</data><data key="e_note">Annotated arrays and/or contiguous windows carrying recurrent family markers.</data></edge><edge id="e3" source="I_5p" target="p96"><data key="e_kind">array