><data key="e_label">Satellite occurrence</data><data key="e_span">3360</data><data key="e_note">Annotated arrays and/or contiguous windows carrying recurrent family markers.</data></edge><edge id="e42" source="II_5p" target="II_unloc_3"><data key="e_kind">bridge</data><data key="e_label">23 bp satellite crossed</data><data key="e_reads">4</data><data key="e_ids">6a278710-be23-46f4-a731-97ce7010c03d,05846a09-f079-4c9f-bbab-57104ee6b86c,1338a409-35c5-4261-9b6e-7aa5bde734bd,80dc7883-eb6a-4d79-80fe-bf5351c23534</data><data key="e_note">Four original ONT molecules uniquely anchor on both sides. One gives the 10,983 bp sequence in the gap-free reviewed join.</data><data key="e_source">ii_iii_open_ports/II23.exact_splices.tsv</data></edge><edge id="e43" source="II_unloc_3" target="II_unloc_1"><data key="e_kind">bridge</data><data key="e_label">Mixed satellite crossed</data><data key="e_reads">1</data><data key="e_ids">1338a409-35c5-4261-9b6e-7aa5bde734bd</data><data key="e_note">The longer ONT read crosses both fragments. An exact-anchor splice uses 2,577 bp of observed DNA.</data><data key="e_source">ii5_chain_extension/PS1017.II5_extended.review.json</data></edge><edge id="e44" source="II_5p" target="G_II5"><data key="e_kind">candidate</data><data key="e_label">Route through shared II satellites</data><data key="e_reads">0</data><data key="e_ids">m64016_201225_182119/116262872/ccs,m64016_201225_182119/27921000/ccs,m64016_201225_182119/40503300/ccs,m64016_201225_182119/54987274/ccs</data><data key="e_note">An installed 7,933 bp graph extension is supported by four HiFi seam reads. The additional route via utg000063l remains a candidate. ONT distal overhang matches several II_unloc_2 placements.</data><data key="e_source">ii5_chain_extension/sequence_support.tsv</data></edge><edge id="e45" source="G_II5" target="II_unloc_4"><data key="e_kind">candidate</data><data key="e_label">Graph alignment</data><data key="e_reads">0</data><data key="e_note">Primary utg000063l aligns across all of II_unloc_4 in reverse orientation. True overlap with the newest II tip remains ambiguous.</data><data key="e_source">p_utg.reference.paf</data></edge><edge id="e46" source="G_II5" target="II_unloc_2"><data key="e_kind">candidate</data><data key="e_label">Graph alignment</data><data key="e_reads">0</data><data key="e_note">Primary utg000063l includes 37,046 bp from II_unloc_2. The ONT overhang has multiple placements in the repeat.</data><data key="e_source">ii5_chain_extension/outward.far_route.paf</data></edge><edge id="e47" source="I_3p" target="III_unloc_1"><data key="e_kind">bridge</data><data key="e_label">Reads enter unlocalized sequence</data><data key="e_reads">15</data><data key="e_ids">m64016_201225_182119/11404042/ccs</data><data key="e_note">HiFi molecules cross the panel boundary into the portion of III_unloc_1 used on I. The family C000043 provides its cap.</data><data key="e_source">deep_junctions.tsv</data></edge><edge id="e48" source="V_5p" target="I_unloc_1"><data key="e_kind">bridge</data><data key="e_label">Reads enter unlocalized sequence</data><data key="e_reads">3</data><data key="e_ids">m64016_201225_182119/134351504/ccs</data><data key="e_note">Direct molecules support the graph transition into sequence formerly labeled I_unloc_1.</data><data key="e_source">deep_junctions.tsv</data></edge><edge id="e49" source="I_3p" target="G_I3"><data key="e_kind">candidate</data><data key="e_label">Alternate longer cap route</data><data key="e_reads">0</data><data key="e_note">C000028 supports a longer primary-contig allele. The assembled I 3′ terminus uses the shorter C000043 path.</data></edge><edge id="e50" source="G_C38" target="V_unloc_1"><data key="e_kind">candidate</data><data key="e_label">Capped fragment contains V_unloc_1</data><data key="e_reads">0</data><data key="e_note">A nearly exact 133 kb graph placement. Molecules support the cap junction on the fragment. Position on a specific chromosome is still ambiguous.</data><data key="e_source">clusters.p_utg.paf</data></edge><edge id="e51" source="III_5p" target="G_C38"><data key="e_kind">candidate</data><data key="e_label">Compatible 20 bp repeat</data><data key="e_reads">0</data><data key="e_note">Correct inward orientation at the capped fragment. The repeat-facing V route shares more distinct oriented 21-mers (352 versus 269). Direct bridge to III 5′ absent in the targeted screen.</data><data key="e_source">ii_iii_open_ports/oriented_marker_comparison.tsv</data></edge><edge id="e52" source="V_3p" target="G_V3"><data key="e_kind">candidate</data><data key="e_label">Primary contig continuation</data><data key="e_reads">0</data><data key="e_note">The review includes the first read-spanned extension. The longer primary contig continues through additional repeats and V_unloc_2.</data><data key="e_source">deep_junctions.tsv</data></edge><edge id="e53" source="G_V3" target="V_unloc_2"><data key="e_kind">candidate</data><data key="e_label">Graph and partial read evidence</data><data key="e_reads">0</data><data key="e_note">A full V_unloc_2 alignment and an approximately 33 kb tail reproduced by raw utg000162l. Tested ONT pairings have competing repeat placements.</data><data key="e_source">ii_iii_open_ports/bridging_molecules.tsv</data></edge><edge id="e54" source="G_V3" target="G_C38"><data key="e_kind">candidate</data><data key="e_label">Compatible 20 bp repeat</data><data key="e_reads">0</data><data key="e_note">Compatible direction. The V graph path is the main competitor for the C000038 fragment.</data><data key="e_source">ii_iii_open_ports/oriented_marker_comparison.tsv</data></edge><edge id="e55" source="X_5p" target="I_5p"><data key="e_kind">candidate</data><data key="e_label">Conflicting ONT read placement</data><data key="e_reads">0</data><data key="e_ids">e10da57f-450f-4578-81e8-6093d1e4fa96</data><data key="e_note">One ONT molecule with an X 5′ repeat placement also has a 7.4 kb cap-adjacent alignment near the accepted I 5′ cap. Whole-read placements compete. This edge records ambiguity.</data><data key="e_source">ONT.X5.whole.paf</data></edge><node id="junction_1"><data key="n_label">I_5p terminal</data><data key="n_type">junction</data><data key="n_status">germline</data><data key="n_note">The original molecule supplies an outward germline junction.</data><data key="n_dist">7744</data><data key="n_coordinate">7744</data><data key="n_families">C000025</data></node><edge id="je1" source="I_5p" target="junction_1"><data key="e_kind">junction</data><data key="e_reads">11</data><data key="e_ids">m64016_201225_182119/44040521/ccs</data><data key="e_note">The original molecule supplies an outward germline junction.</data></edge><node id="junction_2"><data key="n_label">I_3p terminal</data><data key="n_type">junction</data><data key="n_status">germline</data><data key="n_note">The original molecule supplies an outward germline junction.</data><data key="n_dist">6882</data><data key="n_coordinate">11618026</data><data key="n_families">C000043</data></node><edge id="je2" source="I_3p" target="junction_2"><data key="e_kind">junction</data><data key="e_reads">3</data><data key="e_ids">m64016_201225_182119/56754640/ccs</data><data key="e_note">The original molecule supplies an outward germline junction.</data></edge><node id="junction_3"><data key="n_label">II_3p terminal</data><data key="n_type">junction</data><data key="n_status">germline</data><data key="n_note">The original molecule supplies an outward germline junction.</data><data key="n_dist">895</data><data key="n_coordinate">10796031</data><data key="n_families">C000037</data></node><edge id="je3" source="II_3p" target="junction_3"><data key="e_kind">junction</data><data key="e_reads">7</data><data key="e_ids">m64016_201225_182119/149947805/ccs</data><data key="e_note">The original molecule supplies an outward germline junction.</data></edge><edge id="ja3_p96" source="p96" target="junction_3"><data key="e_kind">junction_near_array</data><data key="e